00:10:27,436 --> 00:10:30,149
moved into serious delinquency on an

291
00:10:30,149 --> 00:10:31,653
annual basis.

292
00:10:31,917 --> 00:10:34,667
Let me put the dealership together.

293
00:10:34,727 --> 00:10:36,767
A thin profit on the car.

294
00:10:36,767 --> 00:10:38,731
A thick profit on the loan and

295
00:10:38,731 --> 00:10:40,067
the add-ons.

296
00:10:40,117 --> 00:10:42,859
A steady profit on every repair for

297
00:10:42,859 --> 00:10:43,687
years.

298
00:10:43,817 --> 00:10:45,596
And a law that keeps the door

299
00:10:45,596 --> 00:10:47,437
in the dealer's hands.

300
00:10:47,437 --> 00:10:49,207
The car is the bait.

301
00:10:49,217 --> 00:10:52,005
The customer is the business.

302
00:10:52,250 --> 00:10:54,833
So how do car dealerships really make

303
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:55,950
money?

304
00:10:56,070 --> 00:10:57,692
Not mainly on the car you drive

305
00:10:57,692 --> 00:10:58,900
away in.

306
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:00,489
On the loan you sign for it,

307
00:11:00,489 --> 00:11:02,280
the warranty you add to it,

308
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:04,690
and the service bay you return to.

309
00:11:04,890 --> 00:11:07,000
Knowing that changes how you buy.

310
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,415
Negotiate the price,

311
00:11:08,415 --> 00:11:09,831
but also the rate,

312
00:11:09,831 --> 00:11:11,870
the add-ons and the term.

313
00:11:11,870 --> 00:11:14,359
That is where the dealer's money really

314
00:11:14,359 --> 00:11:15,208
